{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_8aaf18af64054fedb0b9ffb1","type":"tool_result","content":"39e829d306 c: observe a bounded read loop's untested post-loop cursor cleanup (#228)\n3770e18382 Claim polkit .rules files and emit the subject-gate sibling-arm observation (#225)\n37c2b9db32 Merge pull request #224 from vyprai/engine-work/javascript-has-no-working-receiver-type-route-for-source-bin\n63543ac013 lowering: type a JavaScript module global from the writes that fill it\nde1f355594 Merge pull request #222 from vyprai/engine-work/the-c-c-frontend-records-a-call-s-arguments-as-compacted-sou\nad350f7023 engine: keep a call_arg_const fact behind the scope that declares its name\ne25e3b434f engine: carry a C constant string's content to the call that reads it\nbb3f8cfcc0 frontend: claim the .twig extension so Twig template output lowers (#223)\nd074b01590 Merge pull request #220 from vyprai/engine-work/rust-presence-facts-stop-at-the-function-rsstructuredcontext\n9c99369cc5 Merge branch 'main' into engine-work/rust-presence-facts-stop-at-the-function-rsstructuredcontext\n8c2edb2e9f Merge pull request #218 from vyprai/engine-work/internal-extract-lowering-lowering-go-resolvetargets-looks-a\n5048465f68 Merge branch 'main' into engine-work/internal-extract-lowering-lowering-go-resolvetargets-looks-a\n94631d9d4b engine: attribute an instanceof narrowing to the checked type's visibility (#221)\nc65afe5c75 engine: no-frontend-claims-the-gsp-extension-so-a-grails-template-fi (#219)\n2f761171d5 engine: attribute a Rust sibling helper's facts to the function that calls it\ncommit 39e829d3067dcd84d2d68be0fceadca0cee62968\nAuthor: Kiki Luqman Hakiem <4023108+kikihakiem@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Wed Sep 16 11:18:09 2026 +0700\n\n    c: observe a bounded read loop's untested post-loop cursor cleanup (#228)\n    \n    A loop that bounds its cursor in its own condition and breaks out of its\n    own body has two exits, and they leave the cursor in two different places:\n    the break leaves it on the element that matched, the exhausted bound leaves\n    it at or past the last element the range allows. Nothing recorded which one\n    a function's post-loop cleanup assumed. The cleanup written for the break\n    -- step past the match, then store through the cursor -- is out of bounds\n    on the bound's exit, and no fact existed for a binding to name, so the\n    out-of-bounds write was unreachable from the data no matter what the\n    definitions said.\n    \n    The C/C++ frontend now emits analysis.cursor_loop.missing_exit_check from\n    a new walk beside the end-sentinel one, at the loop, carrying the cursor,\n    the loop's own bound as written, how the cleanup first touches the cursor\n    (advance, write_through, advance_and_write_through), and the missing guard.\n    \n    Both halves are read from the tree. The loop half wants a cursor the loop\n    itself reads through (*p, p->f, p[0]) and steps, a relational bound on it\n    in the loop's own condition, and a break that belongs to this loop rather\n    than to a loop or switch nested inside it; a loop missing any of those has\n    one exit or none, and where it leaves the cursor is not in question. The\n    cleanup half is the statements that follow the loop in its own block, read\n    straight-line and locally: the first one to touch the cursor reports when\n    it steps or stores through it, and the window has already ended at any\n    statement that branches, loops or jumps, at a comparison of the cursor --","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2e47c8b-b052-45f8-b9f8-606406eb025a","uuid":"251c36d1-94a6-47b1-9dc6-f5e68831763c","timestamp":"2026-09-16T06:05:23.015Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"39e829d306 c: observe a bounded read loop's untested post-loop cursor cleanup (#228)\n3770e18382 Claim polkit .rules files and emit the subject-gate sibling-arm observation (#225)\n37c2b9db32 Merge pull request #224 from vy