-nonliteral\n// performs, and it is what the last binding reports, on the same family the\n// slots above are named for so the fact and the slot cannot drift apart.\n//\n// The observation is the argument's shape, from the C frontend's\n// call_arg_shape_at tokens (ccExprShape, internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/\n// c.go): `ID` is a variable, a parameter, a member or an element -- the needle\n// is matched as a substring, so `ID.FIELD` and `ID[...]` carry it too -- and\n// `*ID` a dereferenced pointer. A string literal lowers to `STR`, and\n// parenthesised and concatenated literals stay `STR`, so they do not match.\n//\n// va_start exempts the forwarding wrapper. A C function that opens a va_list\n// is variadic and exists to pass its own parameter list on to a va_list-taking\n// formatter, and the format it forwards is its own format parameter, which\n// each of its callers supplies -- that is exactly what __attribute__((format))\n// declares, and Ruby's own headers declare it on wrappers of this shape\n// (RBIMPL_ATTR_FORMAT on raise_generator_error in the json gem, forwarding to\n// rb_vsprintf). Without the exemption every formatted-error helper written\n// the documented way would be reported, and the wrapper is the documented\n// means of adding one to an extension.\n//\n// Residual, false-negative: a format taken straight from a call's result --\n// rb_raise(e, RSTRING_PTR(msg)) -- lowers to `RSTRING_PTR(ID)`, which is not\n// one of these shapes and is not recognised, because the engine's argument\n// shapes cannot enumerate every callee a value might come from. Residual,\n// false-positive: a macro that stands for a literal format is an `ID` to the\n// unparsed tree and a literal to a compiler, which is the one place this\n// check is noisier than -Wformat-nonliteral after preprocessing.\nbinding rubyCapiComputedFormat {\n  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == \"function\" and node.context.language == \"c\"\n    and containsAny(node.context.callArgShapeAt, [\n      \"rb_sprintf:0:ID\", \"rb_sprintf:0:*ID\", \"rb_vsprintf:0:ID\",\n      \"rb_vsprintf:0:*ID\", \"rb_enc_sprintf:1:ID\", \"rb_enc_sprintf:1:*ID\",\n      \"rb_enc_vsprintf:1:ID\", \"rb_enc_vsprintf:1:*ID\", \"rb_raise:1:ID\",\n      \"rb_raise:1:*ID\", \"rb_fatal:0:ID\", \"rb_fatal:0:*ID\",\n      \"rb_bug:0:ID\", \"rb_bug:0:*ID\", \"rb_warn:0:ID\",\n      \"rb_warn:0:*ID\", \"rb_warning:0:ID\", \"rb_warning:0:*ID\",\n    ])\n    and not (node.context.callPath contains \"va_start\")\n  emit issue code.NonliteralFormatString at node\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
