{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260916140931759cd6b5800a47ed","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me write a probe test to see the current behaviour with a variadic wrapper. I'll write it as a temporary Go test in internal/extract (a scratch file I'll shape into the final test). Let me first check `ExtractC` signature and how the wrapper's body sink is lowered.\n\nThe scenario:\n\n```c\nstatic void log_msg(int level, const char *format, ...)\n{\n    va_list ap;\n    va_start(ap, format);\n    vfprintf(stderr, format, ap);\n    va_end(ap);\n}\n\nstatic void report(char *name)\n{\n    log_msg(1, \"scanned %s\", name);\n}\n```\n\nTaint source: `name` (param of report). Question: does taint from the `log_msg` call's arg (at report) reach the `vfprintf` call's arg nodes (specifically `ap`, args[2])?\n\nLet me write the probe and run it. I'll put it in internal/extract as a scratch test file first (not committed until it's the real test).","signature":"9a1d5dfb22464a87a45c1433"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2e47c8b-b052-45f8-b9f8-606406eb025a","uuid":"852c3c2f-635f-4c85-8827-e2ee4091e15f","timestamp":"2026-09-16T06:09:37.551Z"}
