{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202609161411297e0a5919bd0246ae","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No local aide checkout. I know the CVE though: AIDE CVE-2025-54389 — log output sanitization. Let me quickly check the web for the actual patch shape so my test mirrors reality (the wrapper's name and the sink inside). Actually — the rank's test will mirror it; my engine test just needs the *behaviour*. But matching reality helps. Let me do a quick web search for the AIDE commit.\n\nActually, let me not spend too much on this; I know AIDE's logging structure from memory of the project: in AIDE, `src/log.c` historically had:\n\n```c\nvoid log_msg(log_level_t mes_level, const char *format, ...)\n{\n    va_list ap;\n    ...\n    va_start(ap, format);\n    for (each log target) {\n        ...\n        vfprintf(file, format, ap) or vsyslog(...)\n    }\n    va_end(ap);\n}\n```\n\nActually newer AIDE has `log_msg` wrappers with `STANDARD_LOGGING`... Let me do one quick search to confirm the sink function names, because if the wrapper forwards through `vsbrokprintf` or logs via a helper, the shape may differ.","signature":"585d99b82de34030abd28773"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2e47c8b-b052-45f8-b9f8-606406eb025a","uuid":"d1035096-838d-421d-a2bf-b063c5d8982f","timestamp":"2026-09-16T06:11:36.780Z"}
