{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_ce39cb203dea4382836f0385","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AIDE CVE-2025-54389 log control characters commit log_msg\"\n\n**🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"AIDE CVE-2025-54389 log control characters commit log_msg\",\"location\":\"us\"}\n```\n*Executing on server...*\n\n**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"NVD-CVE-2025-54389 - NIST\", \"link\": \"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-54389\", \"content\": \"This issue has been patched in version 0.19.2. A workaround involves configuring AIDE to write the report output to a regular file,\", \"refer\": \"ref_1\"}, {\"title\": \"CVE-2025-54389\"...\n                                                Here are the search results for **AIDE CVE-2025-54389**:\n\n## CVE Overview\n\n**CVE-2025-54389** is an improper output neutralization vulnerability in AIDE (Advanced Intrusion Detection Environment), affecting versions up to and including 0.19.1.\n\n- **NVD (NIST):** [nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-54389](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-54389) — The issue has been **patched in version 0.19.2**. A workaround involves configuring AIDE to write report output to a regular file.\n- **Red Hat CVE database:** [access.redhat.com/security/cve/cve-2025-54389](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/cve-2025-54389) — The flaw allows an attacker to craft a malicious filename containing **terminal escape sequences** to hide the addition or removal of files from the report.\n\n## Technical Details\n\n- **oss-sec mailing list announcement:** [seclists.org/oss-sec/2025/q3/109](https://seclists.org/oss-sec/2025/q3/109) — The vulnerability is caused by **missing output neutralization before printing filenames**, allowing control characters to tamper with or overwrite terminal output.\n- **SecAlerts:** [secalerts.co/vulnerability/CVE-2025-54389](https://secalerts.co/vulnerability/CVE-2025-54389) — Describes it as an improper output neutralization vulnerability.\n- **Trident Stack:** [tridentstack.com/cve/CVE-2025-54389](https://tridentstack.com/cve/CVE-2025-54389) — Notes fixes are available in Debian, Rocky, and Red Hat packages.\n\n## Fix / Commit Information\n\n- **AIDE ChangeLog (GitHub):** [github.com/aide/aide/blob/master/ChangeLog](https://github.com/aide/aide/blob/master/ChangeLog) — Contains the entry: *\"Escape control characters in report and log output (CVE-2025-54389), thanks to Rajesh Pangare for reporting this issue\"* — this is the fix that sanitizes `log_msg` output by escaping control characters.\n- **Ubuntu Security Notice USN-7697-1:** [ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-7697-1](https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-7697-1) — AIDE incorrectly handled filenames (CVE-2025-54389); also covers a related issue where Rajesh Pangare found AIDE incorrectly handled extended file attributes.\n\n**Summary:** An attacker could craft filenames with terminal control/escape characters that AIDE would print unescaped in its reports and logs, allowing log output manipulation. The fix (in AIDE 0.19.2) escapes control characters in both report and log output. For the exact commit, the AIDE GitHub repository's ChangeLog and commit history (github.com/aide/aide) would be the place to look — would you like me to search for the specific commit hash?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2e47c8b-b052-45f8-b9f8-606406eb025a","uuid":"d5431b6a-2917-4850-a012-3f916981545a","timestamp":"2026-09-16T06:12:06.830Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"AIDE CVE-2025-54389 log control characters commit log_msg","results":["**🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"AIDE CVE-2025-54389 log control characters commit log_msg\",\"location\":\"us\"}\n```\n*Executing on server...*","**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"NVD-CVE-2025-54389 - NIST\", \"link\": \"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-54389\", \"content\": \"This issue has been patched in version 0.19.2. A workaround involves configuring AIDE to write the report output to a regular file,\", \"refer\": \"ref_1\"}, {\"title\": \"CVE-2025-54389\"...\n                                                Here are the search results for **AIDE CVE-2025-54389**:\n\n## CVE Overview\n\n**CVE-2025-54389** is an improper output neutralization vulnerability in AIDE (Advanced Intrusion Detection Environment), affecting versions up to and including 0.19.1.\n\n- **NVD (NIST):** [nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-54389](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-54389) — The issue has been **patched in version 0.19.2**. A workaround involves configuring AIDE to write report output to a regular file.\n- **Red Hat CVE database:** [access.redhat.com/security/cve/cve-2025-54389](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/cve-2025-54389) — The flaw allows an attacker to craft a malicious filename containing **terminal escape sequences** to hide the addition or removal of files from the report.\n\n## Technical Details\n\n- **oss-sec mailing list announcement:** [seclists.org/oss-sec/2025/q3/109](https://seclists.org/oss-sec/2025/q3/109) — The vulnerability is caused by **missing output neutralization before printing filenames**, allowing control characters to tamper with or overwrite terminal output.\n- **SecAlerts:** [secalerts.co/vulnerability/CVE-2025-54389](https://secalerts.co/vulnerability/CVE-2025-54389) — Describes it as an improper output neutralization vulnerability.\n- **Trident Stack:** [tridentstack.com/cve/CVE-2025-54389](https://tridentstack.com/cve/CVE-2025-54389) — Notes fixes are available in Debian, Rocky, and Red Hat packages.\n\n## Fix / Commit Information\n\n- **AIDE ChangeLog (GitHub):** [github.com/aide/aide/blob/master/ChangeLog](https://github.com/aide/aide/blob/master/ChangeLog) — Contains the entry: *\"Escape control characters in report and log output (CVE-2025-54389), thanks to Rajesh Pangare for reporting this issue\"* — this is the fix that sanitizes `log_msg` output by escaping control characters.\n- **Ubuntu Security Notice USN-7697-1:** [ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-7697-1](https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-7697-1) — AIDE incorrectly handled filenames (CVE-2025-54389); also covers a related issue where Rajesh Pangare found AIDE incorrectly handled extended file attributes.\n\n**Summary:** An attacker could craft filenames with terminal control/escape characters that AIDE would print unescaped in its reports and logs, allowing log output manipulation. The fix (in AIDE 0.19.2) escapes control characters in both report and log output. For the exact commit, the AIDE GitHub repository's ChangeLog and commit history (github.com/aide/aide) would be the place to look — would you like me to search for the specific commit hash?"],"durationSeconds":30.045611348000005,"searchCount":1}}
