{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202609161417140ccbcf6a453349bf","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`hasParams` compares `fi.paramNames` (ordered, from funcInfo) against `st.Params` (NIR, includes my synthetic). If I exclude the synthetic from `order`/paramNames, then for a variadic function `hasParams(info, st.Params)` compares `[\"level\",\"format\"]` vs `[\"level\",\"format\",\"__varargs__\"]` → lengths differ → false → the overload re-binding path might re-point `info` to a sibling... Wait, this only matters when `len(funcOverloads[qual]) > 1` — two C files declaring the same function name. Then `!hasParams` → true → `overloadForSignature(cands, st.Params, ...)` → looks for a cand whose paramNames exactly equal st.Params (including synthetic) — none (all exclude synthetic) → `own == nil` → info stays. Same as today? Today st.Params = [\"level\",\"format\"], paramNames same → hasParams true → keeps funcQual's pick. After my change, hasParams false → tries overloadForSignature → nil → keeps pick. Behaviour identical (info unchanged), just via a different route. OK — no drift, but fragile. Alternative: pass a filtered params list at the call site... Actually cleaner: since paramNames excludes the synthetic, also compare against a synthetic-free st.Params. I could filter in hasParams call: `hasParams(info, ccParamsWithoutSynthetic(st.Params))`. Hmm — two call sites of hasParams? Just one (4102). But overloadForSignature also calls hasParams(fi, params) with the same slice — filtering at the 4102 call site covers both.\n\nSimplest robust approach: in the FuncDef lowering at 4102, strip nir.CVarargsParam from st.Params before comparing — one helper `withoutSyntheticCVarargs(st.Params)`. Hmm, wait — actually, let me reconsider putting the synthetic INTO paramNames (JS style) after all, because then hasParams matches naturally (paramNames includes synthetic, st.Params includes it), overload selection uses callArity which subtracts... but callArity is used by selectOverloads, and hasParams by the body-binding path. With synthetic in paramNames:\n- hasParams: lengths match (both include synthetic) → true when signatures equal. \n- overloadForSignature: matches cand whose paramNames == st.Params → the variadic one matches only the variadic decl. Better!\n- callArity must subtract the synthetic (else arity counts it as a required param → a call with exactly named-count args wouldn't match, and MORE would... let me check selectOverloads' use).\n\nLet me read selectOverloads to decide.","signature":"dea7fd31246542d49b16fe03"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2e47c8b-b052-45f8-b9f8-606406eb025a","uuid":"f9d85585-8ef9-4f70-8551-1a186aa1146d","timestamp":"2026-09-16T06:17:27.783Z"}
