{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260916143315af3a3557c22e4229","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The diff looks good. One detail to fix: the comment in `exprStmt` says \"the v-formatted call it is handed to, a va_arg\" — reads fine.\n\nOne thing I notice in `ccWithVariadicTailParam`: the guard comment says \"the definition declares `...`\" — but for the text-fallback path, params could ALSO have come from `c.params()` (tree path succeeded) while the tree ALSO has variadic_parameter — the first loop catches that. The fallback \"...\" replacement only triggers when the tree found no variadic_parameter AND the text fallback produced \"...\". Correct.\n\nEdge: `paramsFromSignatureText` runs only when `len(params)==0`; if it yields ONLY \"...\" (function `f(...)`), then `n>0 && params[n-1]==\"...\"` → replace with synthetic → params=[__varargs__]. Good.\n\nEdge: what if the tree path found params AND the body opens va_list AND the tree has variadic_parameter → append. params non-empty. Good.\n\nEdge: `decl == nil && fn` — paramList(fn) walks. Fine.\n\nNow — one more important check. The `va_start` Assign `Value: nir.Name{ID: nir.CVarargsParam}` is emitted for ANY function whose body has va_start — including one where `ccWithVariadicTailParam` did NOT add the synthetic (e.g. non-variadic misuse, or... hmm wait: if the body opens a va_list AND the declaration has `...`, the param IS added. The Assign and the param-adding gate on the same conditions (body opens va_list + variadic). The only divergence: variadic via text-fallback where paramList(decl) exists but has no variadic_parameter node AND params last != \"...\" — e.g. macro-mangled signature `MYLOG_FUNC(void)` expanding... contrived; then Assign references unbound name → orphan node. Acceptable.\n\nNon-variadic function with va_start (UB): ccWithVariadicTailParam returns params unchanged (no variadic_parameter, no \"...\"), but exprStmt still emits the Assign → orphan `__varargs__` Name node. Rare/malformed. Acceptable.\n\nAnother check — `va_start(ap, format)` where args[0] is `&list[0]`-style? destName handles pointer_expression/unary wraps → identifier. va_list decays so it's written bare. Fine.\n\nNow, hmm, one thing about `exprStmt` placement: va_start/va_copy could appear NOT as an expression_statement but nested (e.g. comma operator, or `if (x) va_start(...)`). C requires va_start as a statement (a block-level expression statement) in practice — the C standard says va_start must be in the function executing the variadic call, before any return; compilers require it in statement context. My rewrite only fires in statement position. A va_start in an if-body without braces — `if (c) va_start(ap, f);` — parses as expression_statement inside the if's body? An if without a block has a direct statement child — which is an expression_statement → my rewrite fires. Good.\n\nNow — performance sanity on a large real C codebase. Let me check the benchmarks dir for a C corpus and run a timed scan base-vs-change to make sure nothing pathological (the walk per function_definition is O(body); there are already many such walks). Actually the parsecache invalidates on rebuild, so timing comparisons include cold parse — fine, just observe reasonableness. Is there a real C repo handy? /campaign/bench/Real-Vuln-Benchmark — let me look.","signature":"9a621682d86c43479f272347"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2e47c8b-b052-45f8-b9f8-606406eb025a","uuid":"0d3db5f7-f60d-4415-a4cc-7eb56dc2bbd1","timestamp":"2026-09-16T06:33:33.072Z"}
