for every package except cmd/vyql, whose TestVyqlSpecs carries 23 failures against that published corpus. Those 23 are pre-existing and unrelated: the failure list was captured with the change reverted and again with it applied and the two lists are identical apart from timing digits. gofmt -l over the changed package prints nothing and go vet on the treesitter and lowering packages is clean.\\n\\nSpecs against the batch's own definitions (VYQL_HOME=/campaign/work/rank-2486-1/vyql, 8,562 specs from 2,491 files): exactly one moves -- cve_rank2486_vite_rsc_reference_id_dynamic_import.test.vyql, second block, \\\"rule VYQL-INJ-023 fired but should not have\\\". That block is the gap's own record: it asserts the pre-fix silence of the assignment spelling, its first block (the declaring-initialiser spelling) still passes, and the two differ only in the binding this change fixes. Whoever owns vyql/ has to flip that block's reject to an expect; the definitions are not mine to edit.\\n\\nBenchmarks, both gated in CI, re-scored at HEAD on this machine's corpora: BenchmarkJava OVERALL +1.00, BenchmarkPython OVERALL +0.90 -- the standing figures, so neither gate moves and nothing in benchmarks/RESULTS.md or README.md needs changing. Neither was touched. All 22 owasp-* ports were also scored (VYQL_BENCH_ALL_OWASP=1): +1.00 each, PASS, including owasp-js and owasp-typescript, the two corpora this frontend change actually touches.\\n\\nEnd to end on rank 2486's own repository. The clone at /campaign/work/rank-2486-1/repo was left untouched at the fix commit; a copy was taken to /tmp and checked out at the vulnerable parent c8af971f. Binaries built at base and at HEAD, both driven through campaign-scan:\\n  - Finding set over the whole tree is IDENTICAL: 44 findings either way, 0 added, 0 removed (`vyql diff` reports \\\"identical -- finding-set preserved\\\"). Scan wall time 2.6 s either way.\\n  - The edge the gap names is present at HEAD and absent at base. `vyql graph` at base