   - End git commit messages with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n   - Say plainly in the answer which ranks the change affects beyond the gap's list (blast radius).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - VyQL scanner: Go; tree-sitter frontends → NIR (neutral IR) → lowering → USG graph (nodes `code.Call`, `code.Arg`, `code.Param`, `FLOWS` edges) → bindings/rules/solvers.\n   - Interprocedural taint: `(*lowerer).evalCall` maps call-site Arg nodes to callee Param nodes via `funcInfo.paramNames[i+paramOffset]`; unmapped args get conservative arg→result edge.\n   - JS precedent: synthetic `JSArgumentsParam = \"__arguments__\"` appended to Params of exported functions using `arguments`; routed additively in evalCall; subtracted in `callArity`.\n   - tree-sitter-c grammar: `...` in a parameter list is a named `variadic_parameter` node; `isCParamDecl` only accepts `parameter_declaration`/`optional_parameter_declaration`, so the tail was dropped.\n   - C va_list mechanics: `va_start(ap, last)` opens the tail; `va_copy(dst, src)` re-opens; `va_arg` reads; v-functions (`vfprintf`, `vsyslog`) consume the list. `va_start` is `__builtin_va_start` in stdarg.h; `__va_copy` is old glibc spelling.\n   - AIDE CVE-2025-54389 (CWE-117): filenames with terminal control/escape chars reach report and log output unescaped (fixed 0.19.2). Rank 3007's flow: scan-derived filename → variadic `log_msg(level, fmt, ...)` wrapper → output call inside wrapper body.\n   - Test patterns: `lowerC(t, name, src)` helper (writes temp file, `treesitter.ExtractC`, `lowering.Lower`), `usg.BFS(g, from, \"FLOWS\", 60)` reachability, `usg.ArgPropKey(i)` for call arg slots; source line numbers count the leading newline after the opening backtick.\n   - Env for tests: `VYQL_HOME=/campaign/repos/defs/vyql` (matched defs — all green) vs `VYQL_HOME=/campaign/repos/corpus/vyql` (mid-batch corpus defs — 35 pre-existing spec failures).\n   - Base comparison technique: `git worktree add --detach /tmp/base-check 39e829d306` (scratch, removed after).\n   - Parse cache auto-invalidates (salt derived from running executable).\n   - `campaign-scan . --data-dir <dir> --binary /tmp/vyql-bin/vyql` (needs `--binary` since `vyql` not on PATH).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/campaign/work/engine-.../.task.json` — read; defines the gap (rank 3007).\n   - `internal/extract/nir/nir.go` — **MODIFIED**: added beside `JSArgumentsParam`:\n     ```go\n     // CVarargsParam is a synthetic parameter the C/C++ frontend appends for the\n     // `...` tail of a variadic definition whose body opens a va_list. va_start\n     // binds the list onto it, so the tail arguments a caller passes flow into the\n     // wrapper's own body instead of stopping at the call boundary.\n     const CVarargsParam = \"__varargs__\"\n     ```\n   - `internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go` — **MODIFIED** (3 additions):\n     - In `function_definition` case (after the three params-resolution fallbacks, before `name := c.declName(decl)`):\n       ```go\n       params = c.ccWithVariadicTailParam(params, decl, n, c.field(n, \"body\"))\n       ```\n     - New helpers after `paramList`:\n       ```go\n       func (c *ccConv) ccWithVariadicTailParam(params []string, decl, fn, body *tree_sitter.Node) []string {\n           if body == nil || !c.ccBodyOpensVaList(body) { return params }\n           pl := c.paramList(decl)\n           if pl == nil { pl = c.paramList(fn) }\n           for _, ch := range c.namedChildren(pl) {\n               if c.kind(ch) == \"variadic_parameter\" { return append(params, nir.CVarargsParam) }\n           }\n           // The signature-text fallback spells the tail as a parameter literally named\n           // \"...\"; it stands for the same tail, so it takes the same binding.\n           if n := len(params); n > 0 && params[n-1] == \"...\" {\n               out := append([]string{}, params[:n-1]...)\n               return append(out, nir.CVarargsParam)\n           }\n           return params\n       }\n       var ccVaStartNames = map[string]bool{\"va_start\": true, \"__builtin_va_start\": true}\n       func (c *ccConv) ccBodyOpensVaList(body *tree_sitter.Node) bool { /* walk; call_expression with name in ccVaStartNames */ }\n       ```\n     - In `exprStmt`'s `call_expression` case, inside `if len(args) > 0` after cPropagators/cReaders: a `switch name` — `case \"va_start\", \"__builtin_va_start\":` returns `[nir.Assign{Targets: []string{dst}, Value: nir.Name{ID: nir.CVarargsParam, Loc: c.loc(args[0])}}, nir.ExprStmt{Value: c.expr(inner)}]` (dst via `c.destName(args[0])`); `case \"va_copy\", \"__builtin_va_copy\", \"__va_copy\":` (needs `len(args) > 1`, dst from args[0], args[1] an identifier) returns `[Assign{dst, Name{src}}, ExprStmt]`. The va_start call node is kept (bindings match `callPath contains \"va_start\"`, e.g. ruby_c_api_format_string exemption).\n   - `internal/extract/lowering/lowering.go` — **MODIFIED** (2 additions):\n     - In `evalCall`, right after the JSArgumentsParam block in the resolved-target branch:\n       ```go\n       if varargsParam := target.params[nir.CVarargsParam]; varargsParam != \"\" {\n           for i := len(target.paramNames) - paramOffset; i < len(args); i++ {\n               l.flow(args[i], varargsParam)\n               mapped[i] = true\n           }\n       }\n       ```\n       (First tail arg binds positionally since the synthetic is appended LAST; this loop binds the rest; `mapped[i]=true` removes the conservative arg→result edge for tail args of va_list-opening wrappers.)\n     - In `callArity`: added `if _, ok := fi.params[nir.CVarargsParam]; ok { n-- }` so overload selection is unchanged.\n   - `internal/extract/c_variadic_tail_test.go` — **CREATED** (committed), package `extract_test`; 6 tests: `TestCVariadicTailReachesTheWrapperBody` (log_msg wrapper, va_start+vfprintf, tail arg at `wrapper.c:12` arg2 reaches `wrapper.c:6` arg2), `TestCVariadicTailCarriesEveryTailArgument` (vsyslog, two